# D10 mock — /stateful (state sync). Contract: #37733 §2.8 (FullSession).
# The WHOLE session is one POST (load-balancer affinity). The client streams the
# body from a spooled file; the manager processes + waits for the indexer, then
# answers synchronously. Retries reuse the SAME X-Session-Id; the manager returns
# the cached result (10-min LRU) — proven in the PoC run.

### REQUEST (a full inventory-sync session as one body; may be multi-MB)
POST /stateful HTTP/1.1
Host: 127.0.0.1:27840
protocol-version: 1
Authorization: Wazuh 001:1784311282:9f1c8e5d4a2b1c3d0b61a813cda43396
X-Session-Id: sess-0001
Content-Type: application/octet-stream
Content-Length: 3145728

<FullSession FlatBuffer bytes: Start + DataBatch[] + End>

### RESPONSE (success — synchronous, after indexer confirmation)
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json

{"status":"success","sessionId":"sess-0001","itemsProcessed":3145703}

### RESPONSE (same X-Session-Id replayed — cached, deduplicated)
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json

{"status":"success","sessionId":"sess-0001","itemsProcessed":3145703}

### RESPONSE (indexer timeout)
HTTP/1.1 504 Gateway Timeout

### NOTE
# ReqRet / EndAck{Processing} are REMOVED under HTTPS (#37738 §2/§6): the session
# is atomic, so on error/timeout the agent retries the WHOLE session (same id).
